---
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<header class="intro" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="id">
      <div class="id-head">
        <h1>{site.name}</h1>
        <p class="pron">{site.pronunciation} · he/him</p>
        <p class="contact-line">
          <span class="reduction" title="⊕ = . , ∈ = @">luka ⊕ govedic ∈ nyu ⊕ edu</span>
        </p>
        <p class="addr">
          Desk 330F-7<br>
          Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences<br>
          60 5th Avenue<br>
          New York, NY 10011
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="portrait" src="/profile.jpg" alt="" width="128" height="128" />
    </div>

    <p class="lede">
      I research programming abstractions for better performance, portability, and usability
      for human and agentic programmers, especially in ML and scientific computing.
      My interests span PL, compilers, and formal methods, applied to ML and HPC.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm a PhD student in computer science at NYU's Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences,
      advised by <a href="https://www.saiqianzhang.com/">Sai Qian Zhang</a>.
      I'm also a maintainer of <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm">vLLM</a>,
      where I work on model performance, compilation, kernel fusion, and hardware portability.
      Before NYU, I spent 3 years at Neural Magic (acquired by Red Hat) working on sparse LLM inference
      on GPU and CPU before pivoting to vLLM.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      In my free time, I enjoy playing sports (ultimate frisbee, soccer, skiing, & tennis),
      hiking the Alps, playing board games, and composing <a href="#music"> music</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="links">
      {site.links.map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
